{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And he called the name of the place, etc.</b> This is Mount Moriah, and it was called thus because from fear it became a mountain — for it was at first a valley, and immediately it became a high and towering and elevated mountain. And because at first it was called Shalem, as it is said: ״ומלכי צדק מלך שלם״, and Abraham called it Yira'eh, it is now called Jerusalem, which carries the meaning of both Yira'eh and Shalem." "<b>YHWH will see.</b> The meaning of the verse ״YHWH will see״ is: that it is His will and desire for me to slaughter my son, as He commanded me." "<b>As will be said today, on the mountain of YHWH it will be seen.</b> That is: I know that today many people will say, on the mountain of YHWH it will be seen — even Abraham, does he fear Elohim, that he slaughters his son at the command of the Rock? And when they see us returning, they will say that I did not wish to fulfill the commandment of HaShem; and then it will be seen that the obstruction is not from my side. And it is stated in the Midrash: When the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Abraham, ״Do not send your hand against the boy, and offer the ram in place of your son,״ Abraham did not wish to release him until the Holy One, blessed be He, swore to him that the ram's ashes would be reckoned before Him as though they were Isaac's ashes. And He swore to him, and immediately he lowered him from the altar. And after he lowered him, he said to Him: Give me Your seal on this matter. He said to him: By strict justice I have no obligation to give My seal, since you did not ask for it at the time of the deed, and moreover I have already sworn to you. But I will do kindness with you — to Jacob your grandson I will give it. That which is written: ״תתן אמת ליעקב חסד לאברהם״ — that is: ״You will give אמת,״ which is the seal of the Holy One, blessed be He, to Jacob, ״חסד״ — because of the kindness You said You would do for Abraham."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:52.569450128Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}